  "2026-10-04T19:28:39.241Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: strict full all-status corpus read 2882 of 2882 with zero omissions plus request-specific search and open/in-progress inventories. Historical pm-khdq owns generated allocation overwrite prevention. Historical pm-35w9l2 owns similarity governance. Neither owns the newly reported explicit-ID public typed error contract. GH-1400 source report is retained in full. Remains open and unclaimed; no implementation or live reproduction is claimed."
  "2026-10-06T09:44:16.663Z","harness:codex","TDD: real concurrent explicit-ID creates produce one winner and one loser, but the baseline loser lacks stable code and existing coordinates. Added a structural public SDK/core guard, producer-owned item_already_exists code with canonical id/path, and byte-preservation checks for item plus one-event history across SDK and CLI retries. Generated-ID allocation and similarity governance remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-06T09:50:18.096Z","harness:codex","Compatibility evidence: public surface generation classified exact signature text changes for PmCliErrorContext and PmCliExpectedError. Acknowledged only optional additive code/id/path fields; existing constructors, names, exit classes and required shapes remain compatible. Guard exports are separate additions. Focused create/init suites passed 174 tests. Dependency audit reports no known vulnerabilities and tracked-file secret scan is clean."
  "2026-10-06T10:12:51.046Z","harness:codex","Current linked real-concurrency and structural-guard tests pass. The actual publish tarball was installed in two isolated consumers with npm and bun; both Node and Bun preserve one winning create and expose the losing existing-item conflict through both SDK barrels. CLI retries preserve original item/history bytes, and npx/bunx execute the packed manifest. The stable error ledger and generated catalog now explicitly classify item_already_exists as conflict exit4. Final full coverage/static verification remains pending."
  "2026-10-06T11:49:28.750Z","harness:codex","Local completion: Real concurrent SDK creation has one winner; a cross-type losing retry and CLI retry preserve original document/history bytes; root and core guards also pass in installed Node and Bun consumers. Canonical full suite passes 9789 runnable tests with only two established Windows-only skips. All 764 maintained source files have zero uncovered counts: statements66841/66841; branches51174/51174; functions13809/13809; lines63702/63702. Complete static pipeline, all four TypeScript configurations, 58 token surfaces, docs links, packed artifact and nine-package npx/bunx smoke pass. Bunx smoke uses a fresh owned temporary cache after the host cache symlink was refused; no host cache or gate is weakened. Required current production Sentry/telemetry gate passes with zero blocking issues and finish-error rate2.06% with zero missing error-code rows. Hosted exact-head review remains required before merge; this is implemented local-source evidence and does not claim published registry adoption."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-06T10:28:47.336Z","harness:codex",Cross-bundle SDK recovery must use a stable producer discriminator and validated identity coordinates rather than message wording or instanceof. Create conflicts are emitted under the existing per-ID write lock and name the actual preserved type-folder document. A re-read lets the caller compare intent; returning an existing item automatically would make a separate equivalence decision.
